# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""A hand-written simulation corpus, independent of the template generator.

``tools/generate_synthetic_cn_notes.py`` builds documents that match what the
detectors can already do, so a strict 1.0 there measures agreement with its own
templates. This corpus was written the other way round: real note shapes first
(门急诊 / 住院 / 检验 / 护理 / 手术 / 急诊 / 会诊 / 转科 / 出院), then the
expected PHI marked up, without consulting the detector regexes.

It exists to measure **generalisation**, not to gate CI. Nothing here is a
pass/fail assertion: the point is to see the number, and to see which shapes
the baseline misses. Findings are recorded in
``.internal/simulation-evaluation-2026-09-23.md``.

Every value is synthetic. Names, addresses, phone numbers and identifiers are
constructed; no real patient data appears here.
"""
